Final fix source 55a5f8905c27522f15bc96c32e87b407fc3fcdc3, signed G: one last-admitted cursor plus one retained retry-turn seat. No queue growth or new runtime task.
On a refused eligible seat, retain its turn; later hot offers are refused until it is serviced. A seat that just succeeded cannot reserve the next turn for its own next frame. The next sweep starts at the waiter, or after the last admitted seat. Missing/detached/inactive waiters are cleared before service.
No wait, wire change, capacity increase, PTY throttle, event/generation/checkpoint rule change, or capture/replay algorithm change.
The same named deterministic regression now covers: first hot seat / waiting seat, mid-sweep credit return, hot-seat FIFO, and a detached waiter releasing its turn. Two PTYs, one channel slot; no clock assertion.
Final checks (RUSTC_WRAPPER and RUSTC_WORKSPACE_WRAPPER empty, O0/debug assertions, debuginfo0, two jobs, explicit memory custody):
